+### Index Calculation
+For a contiguous 1D array `_voxelData` of generic type `T`, 3D coordinates $(x, y, z)$ are mapped to a 1D index using row-major ordering (implied by "left-to-right, bottom-to-top, back-to-front" [S2, unofficial] and standard C-style array flattening [S6, unofficial]):
+
 $$
-\text{Index} = x + y \cdot W + z \cdot W \cdot H
+\text{Index}(x, y, z) = x + y \cdot W + z \cdot W \cdot H
 $$
-Where $W, H, D$ are the integer dimensions [S6, unofficial].
 
-**Parameters:**
-- `INVALID_NODE`: $0xFFFFFFFF$ (used in hierarchical variants, not pure dense layout) [S3, unofficial].
-- `ROOT_NODE`: $0$ [S3, unofficial].
-- Voxel size: Often scaled such that edges are $1/8$ unit in length for detail [S1, unofficial].
+Where:
+-   $W$ is Width.
+-   $H$ is Height.
+-   $D$ is Depth (used for bounds checking).
 
